# Implementation Plan: Extract `Entrada` Components

This plan covers the final part of **Phase 4** of the [IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md](file:///Users/miguelbrito/Development/codex/testapp/IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md): extracting the three entry form components out of the monolithic [App.tsx](file:///Users/miguelbrito/Development/codex/testapp/src/App.tsx). 

## User Review Required

> [!WARNING]
> This refactor will move over 300 lines of JSX per module from [App.tsx](file:///Users/miguelbrito/Development/codex/testapp/src/App.tsx) into dedicated component files. While no business logic changes will occur, these components will require many props to be passed down from [App.tsx](file:///Users/miguelbrito/Development/codex/testapp/src/App.tsx) because we haven't implemented context/state slicing yet (Phase 5). This is expected and follows the incremental plan.

## Proposed Changes

We will extract the "Entrada" tab content for all three modules into their respective folders.

---

### DS Module

#### [NEW] [DsEntrada.tsx](file:///Users/miguelbrito/Development/codex/testapp/src/components/ds/DsEntrada.tsx)
Extract rendering logic for `activeModule === 'ds' && activeTab === 'entrada'` from [App.tsx](file:///Users/miguelbrito/Development/codex/testapp/src/App.tsx) lines ~3888-4070.
Props required by this component will include:
- `dsRecentRecords`, `dsStatuses`, `dsOrderedStatuses`, `dsDefaultStatus`
- Form state: `dsEntryForm`, `setDsEntryForm`
- Actions: [submitDsEntry](file:///Users/miguelbrito/Development/codex/testapp/src/App.tsx#1918-1952), [saveNewDsEntry](file:///Users/miguelbrito/Development/codex/testapp/src/App.tsx#1953-1957), [handleDsEntryInput](file:///Users/miguelbrito/Development/codex/testapp/src/App.tsx#1869-1872)
- Suggestions/options: `dsGestoraFilterOptions`, `dsProponentesSuggestions`, etc.
- Navigation/selection: `setActiveTab`, `setSelectedDsRecordId`

#### [MODIFY] [App.tsx](file:///Users/miguelbrito/Development/codex/testapp/src/App.tsx)
Replace the inline DS Entry JSX with `<DsEntrada {...props} />`.

---

